  "license": "Dataset and documentation CC BY 4.0 per fixed README. Code and hardware codebase MIT per README.",
  "queries": [
    "open source robot actuator dynamometer testbench data logs motor output torque github load cell quasi direct drive characterization dataset",
    "GitHub robot actuator motor dynamometer transmission efficiency torque sensor harmonic cycloidal test data CSV robot gear actuator benchmark",
    "open leg actuator characterization torque bandwidth sample data series elastic actuator experiment supplementary data bandwidth GIM6010 AK80 GitHub"
  ],
  "evidence": "Full pinned repository tree, every bench test CSV (135), static calibration and software that generates/consumes these records. HIL trajectory files were inventoried but their values were not inspected. This is a repository record, without a peer-reviewed publication identifier verified here.",
  "findings": [
    "Five test families respectively have 3610/2372/4808/11964/3004 numeric rows. All 25758 core rows have finite time, position request, speed response, Iq and torque readback. Maximum absolute difference between torque readback and 0.55 × Iq is at most 0.00007501 Nm. No selected row has |Iq| ≥10 A. The 11 static calibration levels show the same calculation to 0.0000651 Nm.",
    "The 25 test-5 runs include five replicates per labeled load. On the +50 degree commanded segment the within-run maximum positive speed has medians of 381.875/385.625/386.250/385.000/396.250 degrees/s across the five load levels 0/0.5/1/1.5/2 Nm. This statistic has no monotonic decline.",
    "In the producer, torque_cmd_Nm records the unsigned nominal condition throughout each run. At the step the code passes negative load as opposing feedforward. The per-sample voltage and current and optical-encoder response are useful; the signed actuator net torque and unconstrained torque are not recorded.",
    "The current-to-torque calculation is explicit in odrive_ascii_interface.py. process_phase1_bench_data.m lines 538–539 assign tau_stall_est=2.45 and gamma_est=4.5 as constants."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The readback shares the current signal used to compute it and cannot validate a shaft-torque calibration on its own. Rate-limited behavior and a physical torque ceiling require additional evidence.",
    "Readme identifies the bench acquisitions as physical; the acquisition interface can also run serial or mock mode. The static calibration header says COM3, while individual dynamic CSV files have no serial/mock flag.",
    "Forward peaks use the +50° step subset, not the MATLAB full-file peak or a fitted speed ceiling."
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "steering-bench-runs.csv",
    "steering-static-calibration.csv"
  ],
